workedExample:
1. Freeing a node invalidates the memory holding its `left` and `right` pointers.
2. In this implementation, both recursive child calls therefore run before free(n).
3. Children before parent is exactly post-order: left, right, node.

```c
void free_tree(Node *n) {
    if (!n) return;
    // Children before their parent.
    free_tree(n->left);
    free_tree(n->right);
    free(n);
}
```

The same reasoning explains why `rm -r` deletes a directory's contents before the directory.
